.TH "AUDIO-STATUS.SH" "1" "2026-11-06" "Homelab ops"
.SH NAME
audio-status.sh \- Report audio status for the configured Waybar module.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B audio-status.sh
[arguments]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Report audio status for the configured Waybar module.
Established names and consumer paths are preserved. No hardware or service action was executed for documentation verification.
.SH INTERFACE
.SS /home/iragonforce/.config/hypr/scripts/waybar/audio-status.sh
Source: hosts/tensor/files/.config/hypr/scripts/waybar/audio-status.sh
.nf
mode="${1:-value}"
case "$1" in
awk -v sink="$1" '
$1 == "Name:" { current = $2 }
current == sink && $1 == "Description:" {
local sink="$1"
local name="$2"
pactl get-sink-volume "$1" 2>/dev/null | grep -oE '[0-9]+%' | head -1 | tr -d '%'
pactl get-sink-mute "$1" 2>/dev/null | awk '{ print $2 }'
MODE="$mode" python3 - "$1" "$2" "$3" <<'JSONPY'
"text": sys.argv[1],
"tooltip": sys.argv[2],
.fi

.SH DEPENDENCIES
Use the interpreter in the source shebang and the existing host packages and services referenced in that source. Host configuration and private credentials remain on their original host.
.SH OPERATIONS
Before changing behavior, inspect inventory/audit-2026-11-06/tensor.json for recorded consumers and the source above for exact dependency paths. Never invoke a power, desktop, network, credential, notification, or storage operation merely to test it.
.SH SOURCE
